# Copy to .env and fill in — required for any `llm-yuki compile` run that reaches an LLM-backed stage
# (Extractor.compile_wiki_pages, Validator.content_validate, Fixer.llm_periodic_fix).
# See root ARCHITECTURE.md §2.1/§5: this pipeline targets an OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions API,
# either OpenRouter or a self-hosted OpenAI-compatible server — never a vendor-specific native SDK.
# All three variables are required; missing any of them fails at CLI startup, not mid-batch.

# Option A: OpenRouter (https://openrouter.ai/) — pick any model it serves
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
LLM_MODEL=openrouter/some-provider/some-model

# Option B: a self-hosted OpenAI-compatible server (e.g. vLLM, Ollama) — uncomment and adjust instead
# OPENAI_API_KEY=unused-but-required-by-the-client
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1
# LLM_MODEL=your-locally-served-model-name

# Optional: operational console log level (src/llm_yuki/logging.py) — not required, defaults to INFO.
# One of the standard logging module level names (DEBUG/INFO/WARNING/ERROR/CRITICAL).
# LLM_YUKI_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG
